{"unit":12,"items":72,"pass":50,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 12","tracks":{"a121":"Track_12.1.mp3"},"SEGS":{"all":["a121",3.92,162.79]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Final Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 12 &middot; Final Test</div>\n      <h2>The whole level</h2>\n      <p>This is the last assessment of the course. Eight parts, <b>72 questions</b>, drawn from <b>all twelve units</b>, not only from Unit 12. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>50 out of 72</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, and at this level they matter as much as the rest. Allow yourself ninety minutes. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-final\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary across the level &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;14</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">The poster was on every wall in the city for a month. It was extremely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">replaceable</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">temporary</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">memorable</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">He never gives in during a negotiation. He is the most&hellip; person I know.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">determined</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">careless</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">underdressed</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">Nobody had heard of that district ten years ago. It was completely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">closed off</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">unheard of</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">run-down</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">A good negotiator does not argue &mdash; they try to&hellip; the objection.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">criticize</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">blame</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">overcome</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5</span><span class=\"body\">She never says anything to anybody else. I&hellip; her completely.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">trust</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">persuade</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">resist</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match each verb to the phrase it goes with. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">6&ndash;10</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"f1\">win</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"f2\">rely</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"f3\">take</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"f4\">keep</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"f5\">make</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"f3\" data-short=\"somebody seriously\">somebody seriously</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"f5\" data-short=\"progress\">progress</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"f1\" data-short=\"somebody over\">somebody over</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"f4\" data-short=\"in touch\">in touch</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"f2\" data-short=\"on somebody\">on somebody</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the right preposition.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">She asked whether I was aware <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"of\" data-why=\"<b>Aware of</b> something.\"> the objection.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">He wanted to know what the decision depended <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"on\" data-why=\"<b>Depend on</b> &mdash; and the preposition stays at the end.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">They asked me whether I was interested <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"in\" data-why=\"<b>Interested in</b> something.\"> the offer.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">Nobody is capable <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"of\" data-why=\"<b>Capable of</b> doing something.\"> doing that alone.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar across the level &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 15&ndash;34</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">I&hellip; her since we were at school together.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">know</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">have known</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">am knowing</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">While he&hellip; for the path, he fell into a stream.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">looked</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">had looked</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">was looking</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">It&hellip; since Tuesday, and the ground still has not dried.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">has been raining</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">has rained once</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">is raining</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">The whole campaign&hellip; by five thousand strangers.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">funded</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">was funded</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">has funding</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">If he&hellip; the plane, nobody would ever have heard of him.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">didn&rsquo;t steal</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">wouldn&rsquo;t have stolen</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">hadn&rsquo;t stolen</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">The car&hellip; drives itself is already on the roads.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">that</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">who</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">whose</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">Look at the clothes. It&hellip; a modern painting.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">must be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">might be</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">can&rsquo;t be</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">I would recommend&hellip; it in the original language.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">to watch</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">watching</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">watch</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the verb in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>not / see</i>) I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"haven't seen|have not seen\" data-why=\"From the past up to now &rarr; present perfect.\"> her since the wedding.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>already / leave</i>) By the time we arrived, they <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"had already left\" data-why=\"Earlier than another past point &rarr; past perfect.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>manage</i>) After three attempts she <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"managed to finish\" data-why=\"<b>Manage to</b> + base verb, for success after difficulty.\"> the whole course.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>be able</i>) I hope I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"will be able to|'ll be able to\" data-why=\"<i>Can</i> has no future form &rarr; <b>will be able to</b>.\"> join you next month.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>test</i>) The prototype <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"is being tested\" data-why=\"Happening around now &rarr; present continuous passive.\"> at the moment.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">If it <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"rains\" data-why=\"No <b>will</b> after <i>if</i> &mdash; the condition takes the present simple.\">, we’ll stay in.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">My phone, <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"which\" data-why=\"After a comma only <b>which</b> is possible, never <i>that</i>.\"> I bought in May, is already broken.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">You really <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"should have asked\" data-why=\"<b>Should have</b> needs the past participle: <i>should have asked</i>.\"> before you shared it.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">She asked me what <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"I wanted\" data-why=\"A reported question has no inversion: <i>what I wanted</i>.\"> from the session.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">I am not brave, so I am not a firefighter.<br>If I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"were braver, i'd be a firefighter|were braver i would be a firefighter|was braver i'd be a firefighter\" data-why=\"An imagined present &rarr; past form + <b>would</b>.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">Somebody stole my bike last night.<br>My bike <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"was stolen last night\" data-why=\"Nobody knows who &rarr; passive, doer left out.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">He said: &ldquo;I saw the advert yesterday.&rdquo;<br>He said he <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"had seen the advert the day before\" data-why=\"One step back, and <i>yesterday</i> becomes <b>the day before</b>.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;44</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The sign that told the truth</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">A hospital in Denmark cut missed appointments by more than a third. It did not send a single extra reminder.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>Missed appointments are one of the most expensive small problems in medicine. A patient who does not arrive costs a slot that could have gone to somebody else, and the standard answer &mdash; more reminders, by letter, then by text, then by both &mdash; produces surprisingly little. By 2016 one Danish hospital had been sending three reminders per appointment for four years, and the rate had barely moved.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>What worked was one sentence. The reminder had said: <i>Please call us if you cannot attend.</i> It was changed to: <i>Nine out of ten patients call us if they cannot attend.</i> Nothing else about the system was altered. Within a year, missed appointments had fallen by thirty-eight per cent, and the effect was still there when researchers checked again three years later.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>The explanation is uncomfortable for anybody who likes to think decisions are made by weighing reasons. People are strongly influenced by what they believe other people do, and a request tells you only what is wanted, while a description tells you what is normal. The first version implied that calling was an effort somebody was asking of you. The second implied that not calling would make you unusual.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>The technique has limits, and the researchers who publish it are careful about them. It only works if the sentence is true; a hospital where three out of ten patients call cannot honestly write the second version, and inventing the figure would be both dishonest and, once people noticed, useless. It also works less well the more the behaviour costs. Nobody has yet changed a housing decision or a career with a well-worded sentence.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">E</span>What has changed is what counts as a first attempt. Twenty years ago a public body that wanted people to do something wrote a rule, and then, if the rule was ignored, wrote a stronger one. Now it is normal to test the wording first. That is a smaller idea than it sounds and, in a system where a missed appointment costs about a hundred euros, an unusually cheap one.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">What did the hospital change?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the number of reminders it sent</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the times appointments were offered</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">one sentence in the reminder</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">According to paragraph C, why did the second version work better?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">it described what most people already do</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">it was shorter and easier to read</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">it threatened a penalty</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">The hospital had been sending three reminders for four years. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph A says exactly that.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">The effect had disappeared by the time researchers checked again. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: it was <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Other hospitals in Denmark have copied the change. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"Other hospitals are never mentioned.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">The technique works equally well for very important decisions. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph D: it works <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last four questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">Why do the researchers insist the sentence must be true?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">because a false one is illegal in Denmark</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">because inventing the figure would be dishonest and would stop working</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">because patients check the statistics themselves</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, &ldquo;uncomfortable for anybody who likes to think decisions are made by weighing reasons&rdquo; suggests that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">we are influenced by other people more than we would like to admit</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">reasons never influence anybody at all</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the research has been rejected by other scientists</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">What does paragraph E say has changed?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the cost of a missed appointment</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the number of rules that public bodies write</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">that testing the wording is now a normal first step</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44</span><span class=\"body\">Which sentence best describes the writer&rsquo;s attitude?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">enthusiastic, with no reservations</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">interested, but careful about how far it goes</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">hostile to the whole idea</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 45&ndash;52</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('all',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> The advert I cannot forget &middot; three speakers\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 12.1</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What was each advert about?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">45</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 1 <select data-answer=\"lights\" data-why=\"Speaker 1 describes the Earth Hour advert about switching a light off.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"homeless\">homeless people</option><option value=\"texting\">texting while driving</option><option value=\"lights\">switching lights off to save energy</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">46</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 2 <select data-answer=\"homeless\" data-why=\"Speaker 2 describes homeless people presenting the weather.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"homeless\">homeless people</option><option value=\"lights\">switching lights off to save energy</option><option value=\"texting\">texting while driving</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">47</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 3 <select data-answer=\"texting\" data-why=\"Speaker 3 describes the driving-school advert about texting.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"homeless\">homeless people</option><option value=\"texting\">texting while driving</option><option value=\"lights\">switching lights off to save energy</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the notes with one word.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 1 &mdash; what came towards the three men: a huge cloud of <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"moths|moth\" data-why=\"A huge cloud of <b>moths</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">49</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 2 &mdash; homeless people were asked to present the <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"weather\" data-why=\"They presented the <b>weather</b> on television.\"> on television.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">50</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 3 &mdash; the instructor told the learners that a new <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"law\" data-why=\"A new <b>law</b> had been passed.\"> had been passed.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">51</span><span class=\"body\">What do all three adverts have in common?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">all of them are funny</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">all of them were shown at the cinema</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">none of them sells a product, and each shows a consequence</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">52</span><span class=\"body\">Speaker 3 says &ldquo;No one likes being told not to do something.&rdquo; He is arguing that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">showing what happens works better than giving an instruction</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">driving instructors should be stricter</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">laws never change behaviour</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language across the level &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 53&ndash;62</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits the situation.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">53</span><span class=\"body\">You want to disagree with a colleague without ending the conversation.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">That is completely wrong.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">I see what you mean, but&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">I could not agree more.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">54</span><span class=\"body\">You have to move a meeting with a client, in writing.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Thursday any good?</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Something has come up, sorry!</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Would it be possible to reschedule for Thursday afternoon?</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">55</span><span class=\"body\">You did not understand a word your manager used.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Sorry, could you explain what you mean by that?</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">In other words, that.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Please find attached.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">56</span><span class=\"body\">You are apologizing for something you actually did wrong.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">I am sorry if anybody was offended.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">It was entirely my fault, and I should never have sent it.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">I am sorry you feel that way.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">57</span><span class=\"body\">You are giving the final judgement in an essay.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">One major advantage is that&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">First of all, some background.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">On balance, the case for a full ban is weaker than the case for limiting one.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Spoken, or written? Sort each line.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">58&ndash;61</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Spoken\">What do you reckon?</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Written\">It is widely argued that&hellip;</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Spoken\">Honestly, just watch it. Trust me.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Written\">Despite failing at first, it has become a classic.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Spoken\"><h5>Spoken</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Written\"><h5>Written</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the five paragraphs of the essay in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">62</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"z4,z1,z3,z5,z2\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"z1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">One major advantage of allowing it is money: much of what children watch is paid for by advertisers.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"z2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">On balance, the case for a full ban is weaker than the case for limiting one.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"z3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">A significant drawback, however, is that the youngest children cannot tell an advert from a programme.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"z4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Advertising to children is banned in Sweden and almost unrestricted elsewhere, which suggests the question is genuinely difficult.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"z5\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">The second disadvantage is pressure: the argument arrives at home, and the advertiser is not in the room for it.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 63&ndash;72</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Report what was said or asked.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">63</span><span class=\"body\">&ldquo;The campaign is working.&rdquo;<br>She claimed that the campaign <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"was working\" data-why=\"Present continuous &rarr; past continuous.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">64</span><span class=\"body\">&ldquo;I have never used that brand.&rdquo;<br>He said he <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"had never used that brand\" data-why=\"Present perfect &rarr; past perfect, and <i>that</i> stays.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">65</span><span class=\"body\">&ldquo;Do you agree with me?&rdquo;<br>She asked <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"whether i agreed with her|if i agreed with her\" data-why=\"A yes/no question &rarr; <b>whether</b> or <i>if</i>, and no inversion.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">66</span><span class=\"body\">&ldquo;Why did you change your mind?&rdquo;<br>He asked me <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"why i had changed my mind\" data-why=\"No inversion, and past simple &rarr; past perfect.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Every gap comes from a different unit of the course.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Kamila</b>Did you watch the advert everybody is arguing about?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Twice. I <select data-answer=\"have never seen\" data-why=\"Experience up to now &rarr; present perfect. <b>have never seen</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>never saw</option><option>am never seeing</option><option>have never seen</option></select> anything quite like it.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Kamila</b>My brother says it is manipulative.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"That&rsquo;s a fair point,\" data-why=\"Concede before disagreeing. <b>That&rsquo;s a fair point,</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>That&rsquo;s a fair point,</option><option>He&rsquo;s completely wrong,</option><option>I couldn&rsquo;t agree more,</option></select> but every advert is. The interesting question is whether it is true.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Kamila</b>Who paid for it?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>A charity. The whole thing <select data-answer=\"was funded\" data-why=\"A finished past event in the passive. <b>was funded</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>funded</option><option>was funded</option><option>has funding</option></select> by donations, apparently.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Kamila</b>And it changed nothing.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>I would not say that. If nobody <select data-answer=\"had filmed\" data-why=\"An unreal past condition &rarr; past perfect. <b>had filmed</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>filmed</option><option>had filmed</option><option>would have filmed</option></select> it, the story would have died in a week. And they have been running it for three years now.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Kamila</b>So what would you do in their place?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>If I <select data-answer=\"were\" data-why=\"An imagined present &rarr; <b>were</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>were</option><option>am</option><option>will be</option></select> running it, I would show the consequence and say nothing at all. <select data-answer=\"On balance,\" data-why=\"Introduces a weighed judgement. <b>On balance,</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Firstly,</option><option>On the other hand,</option><option>On balance,</option></select> that is what the good ones do.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 180&ndash;220 words. Give yourself thirty-five minutes. This is the longest thing you will write at this level.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Write an advantages-and-disadvantages essay on <b>one</b> of these:<br>&mdash; Should advertising aimed at children be banned?<br>&mdash; Should everybody have the right to work from home?<br>&mdash; Should competitive sport be part of every school timetable?<br><br>Open by showing that the question is genuinely contested. Give the advantages, with evidence. Give the drawbacks, with evidence. Finish with a conclusion that <b>narrows</b> the question instead of repeating it.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"&hellip; is banned in&hellip; and almost unrestricted&hellip;, which suggests the question is genuinely difficult.   One major advantage is&hellip;   There is also an argument about&hellip;   A significant drawback, however, is&hellip;   The second disadvantage is&hellip;   On balance,&hellip;\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your essay must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>an opening that shows the question is contested, not a definition</li>\n        <li>at least two advantages and two drawbacks, each with something behind it</li>\n        <li>evidence &mdash; a figure, a place, a case &mdash; not four more adjectives</li>\n        <li>no spoken phrases: no <i>What do you reckon</i>, no <i>loads of people</i></li>\n        <li>a conclusion that narrows the question and introduces no new argument</li>\n        <li>at least four different structures from the level: a passive, a conditional, a relative clause, a perfect form</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; three parts, four minutes</b><span>The final assessment</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A &middot; extended turn.</b> Talk for ninety seconds about something that changed your mind. What did you use to think? What happened? What do you think now?<br><b>Part B &middot; both sides.</b> Argue both sides of the essay question you chose, then say which case you find stronger and why.<br><b>Part C &middot; interaction.</b> Somebody disagrees with your conclusion. Half agree with them twice, then hold your ground once, and finish with one sentence beginning <i>On balance</i> that you could both accept.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>Part A: <b>used to</b>, a narrative past form, and a present perfect</li>\n        <li>Part B: at least one conditional and one passive, doing real work</li>\n        <li>Part C: two different softeners before any disagreement</li>\n        <li>throughout: report at least one thing somebody else said to you</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>I used to think&hellip; &middot; What changed it was&hellip; &middot; I&rsquo;ve believed that ever since&hellip; &middot; One major advantage is&hellip; &middot; A significant drawback is&hellip; &middot; I see what you mean, but&hellip; &middot; That&rsquo;s a fair point, although&hellip; &middot; She told me that&hellip; &middot; On balance&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record all three parts, play them back, and mark yourself against the list below.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my opening shows the question is contested instead of defining it</li>\n        <li>every advantage and drawback has evidence behind it</li>\n        <li>my conclusion narrows the question and adds no new argument</li>\n        <li>no spoken phrase found its way into the essay</li>\n        <li>I used a passive, a conditional, a relative clause and a perfect form</li>\n        <li>I spoke for ninety seconds without stopping to translate</li>\n        <li>I argued the side I disagree with as well as my own</li>\n        <li>I half agreed twice before I disagreed once</li>\n        <li>I reported something somebody else had said, one step back</li>\n        <li>I finished with one sentence both sides could accept</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"done-card\">\n      <h3>That is the end of the course</h3>\n      <p>Thirty-six lessons, twelve units, twelve assessments. If you passed this one, you have finished the Intermediate level. If you did not, look at which part cost you the marks &mdash; the parts are deliberately separate so that you can see it &mdash; and go back to those three lessons before you take it again.</p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}